# Every line in the game, by title. Chapters open a title with
# show_dialogue("title"); talking to someone opens talk_<name>; looking at an
# artifact opens artifact_<id>. Each line's [ID:...] names its voice clip
# (voice/<speaker>/<ID>.mp3), made by tools/voice/generate.py. Leave the IDs
# off new lines: tools/voice/build_manifest.py adds them.

~ intro_jerusalem
narrator: Many years ago, my family and I lived in Jerusalem. My father, a prophet of God, saw in a vision that Jerusalem would be destroyed. [ID:MANY_YEARS_AGO_MY_FAMILY_AND_A2D619]
narrator: We left our home and traveled in the wilderness for many years. [ID:WE_LEFT_OUR_HOME_AND_TRAVELED_1CC3F1]
=> END

~ intro_bountiful
narrator: The Lord led us to a land which we called Bountiful, as it had much fruit and honey and was along the seashore. [ID:THE_LORD_LED_US_TO_A_LAND_22D35B]
narrator: There I and my family built a ship and loaded it with enough provisions to cross the sea. [ID:THERE_I_AND_MY_FAMILY_BUILT_A_8539F9]
=> END

~ talk_sheep
sheep: Baa-aa-aa! [i](The sheep keeps chewing and stares at you.)[/i] [ID:BAA_AA_AA_I_THE_SHEEP_KEEPS_CH_495A30]
=> END

~ talk_chicken
chicken: Bawk! Bawk, bawk... BAWK! [i](She seems to have a lot to say.)[/i] [ID:BAWK_BAWK_BAWK_BAWK_I_SHE_SEEM_1B9313]
=> END

~ talk_goat
goat: Maaa! [i](The goat tries to nibble your sleeve.)[/i] [ID:MAAA_I_THE_GOAT_TRIES_TO_NIBBL_57AA79]
=> END
